.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taurctl-reset-password 1  "taurctl-reset-password " 
.SH NAME
taurctl\-reset\-password \- Reset a forgotten password
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaurctl reset\-password\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reset a forgotten password
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Server URL (overrides TAUR_SERVER and the config file)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Config directory (default: $TAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print raw JSON
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin instead of prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
taurctl\-reset\-password\-request(1)
Email a reset link to the account\*(Aqs address
.TP
taurctl\-reset\-password\-confirm(1)
Set a new password with the token from the reset mail (prompts for the password)
.TP
taurctl\-reset\-password\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
